{title: Woman del Callao}
{artist: Un Solo Pueblo}
{year: 1987}
{key: Cm}
{time: 4/4}

{define: C# base-fret 1 frets 1 1 1 4}
{define: Cm base-fret 1 frets 0 3 3 3}
{define: Fm7 base-fret 1 frets 1 3 1 3}
{define: Fm6 base-fret 1 frets 1 2 1 3}
{define: G7 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 1 2}
{define: Fm base-fret 1 frets 1 0 1 3}

[C#]·  · · · | [Cm]·  · · · | [C#]·  · · · | [Cm]·  · · ·

{start_of_chorus: Coro (x4)}
Tiene [Cm]mucho hunt, tiene [Fm7]mucho tempo
Tiene [Fm6]mucho down, [G7] woman[Cm] del callao
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verso}
It’s a [C#]custom to love the man going to El [Cm]Callao
All the [C#]woman has the calypso into the [Cm]blood
When you [C#]go you will like to living dancing in [Cm]this paradise
Every [Fm]time, aha[G7]ha aha[Cm]ha
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Repetir desde el principio al menos una vez más}

{start_of_verse: Outro (x4)}
Tiene [Cm]mucho hunt, tiene [Fm7]mucho tempo
